# FrilOstrichChallenge

# ============================================================================================
# THE WORLDS GO UP THROUGH GIT LFS, NOT THROUGH THIS FILE. See .gitattributes.
#
# They were ignored here briefly, on the grounds that GitHub refuses any file over 100MB and
# each world holds a 134MB dtm.raw. That reasoning was right about the limit and wrong about
# the free LFS allowance, which is 10GB of storage and 10GB of bandwidth a month rather than
# the 1GB assumed. The worlds fit.
#
# WHAT IS IGNORED INSTEAD is the half of each world the game builds for itself on first load.
# ChunkProviderGenerateWorldFromRaw has a processFiles coroutine that writes dtm_processed.raw
# while the loading screen says "Processing world files", and getFilenameDTM falls back to
# dtm.raw when the processed one is absent. generateHalfResTexture does the same job for the
# splat textures. None of it is authored, all of it is cache, and it is 140MB per world.
#
# TESTED IN GAME, 27 Oct 2026, 3.4.0 (b6). The five generated files were moved out of the
# Wasteland world and a new game started on it. The log reads:
#
#     Calculating world hashes took 232 ms (world size 132 MiB)     <- before
#     Processing world files
#     Calculating world hashes took 365 ms (world size 265 MiB)     <- after
#     Loading and creating dtm raw file took 13588ms
#
# The game rebuilt every one of them itself, the world doubled on disk, and checksums.txt was
# recalculated without a word of complaint. Thirteen seconds, once, on first load. Fril: "it
# loaded fine and the files we took out were regenerated".
# ============================================================================================
Mods/OstrichChallenge/worlds/**/dtm_processed.raw
Mods/OstrichChallenge/worlds/**/*_processed.png
Mods/OstrichChallenge/worlds/**/*_half.png
Mods/OstrichChallenge/worlds/**/main.ttw.bak

# THE PACKAGED MOD IS A RELEASE ASSET, NOT A REPO FILE.
# Area 7's Mods.zip is 707MB and the Hospital's is 954MB. Neither of those repos has a
# .gitignore, so in both of them that zip is sat there untracked waiting for a careless
# "git add .".
Mods.zip
*.zip

# RUNTIME OUTPUT, NOT MOD CONTENT.
# occupancy_path.csv is what "occ dir path on" writes, one row per tick of a recorded route.
# It is a debugging artefact and the mod neither reads it nor needs it.
#
# NOTE occupancy_building.txt IS NOT IGNORED AND MUST NOT BE. The mod loads it from its own
# folder on startup (OstrichChallenge.cs sets Building.FilePath to it) and it carries the
# floor heights, the home spot, reception, the entrances, the laptop, the car and the shutter.
# Without it the mod does not know the shape of the building. It is content, not output.
occupancy_path.csv

# Development notes. These live in the working folder and must never reach a release.
zzzzzzHelp_Docs/
Recordings/
DEVLOG*.md
DEMO_*.md
Demolisher_State_Table.html

# Build output and local scratch
/tmp/
*.dll.mdb
*.pdb

# Windows and editor leftovers
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.bak
*.tmp
~$*

# Fireworks working files. The exported PNGs are what the mod ships; the .png source files
# Fireworks saves alongside them are working documents and do not belong in a release repo.
# Remove this line if you decide you want the sources version-controlled after all.
*.fw.png
